ta","data":[{"unit":1,"title":3,"area":95,"prev":27,"next":97,"titles":99,"firmware":269},{"id":2,"title":3,"aliases":4,"area":5,"order":12,"path":13,"context":14,"summary":21,"status":22,"firmware":23,"facts":28,"procedures":61,"parameters":75,"related":76,"body":84,"sources":85,"official_url":32,"controls":93},"mix.overview","Mix mode",[5,6,7,8,9,10,11],"mix","mixer","mixing","mixer mode","signal flow","master bus","master chain",0,"knowledge/manual/units/mix/overview.md",{"modes":15,"screens":16},[5],[17,18,19,20],"M1","M2","M3","M4","Mix mode sets each track's level, pan and FX sends on `M1` and runs the master chain — EQ on `M2`, saturator on `M3`, group levels, compressor and output level on `M4`.","current",{"min":24,"changed_in":25,"guide_version":26,"verified_on":27},"1.0.9",[],"1.1.15",null,[29,34,38,41,46,50,53,56],{"id":30,"text":31,"source":32,"firmware_min":27,"verified_on":27,"confidence":33},"what","Mix mode is where you balance the project — levels, pans and FX sends per track, plus EQ and compression on the master.","https://teenage.engineering/guides/op-xy/mix#arrange","official",{"id":35,"text":36,"source":37,"firmware_min":27,"verified_on":27,"confidence":33},"toggle","Pressing `mix` while already in mix mode flips between the instrument tracks and the auxiliary tracks; both can be mixed.","https://teenage.engineering/guides/op-xy/mix#levels-pans-and-sends",{"id":39,"text":40,"source":37,"firmware_min":27,"verified_on":27,"confidence":33},"leds","A track key selects the track to adjust; instrument tracks light white and auxiliary tracks red.",{"id":42,"text":43,"source":44,"firmware_min":27,"verified_on":27,"confidence":45},"per-scene","A track's level and pan belong to the pattern it plays, as part of that pattern's sound, while each scene keeps the mutes; so a scene changes the balance by switching patterns or mutes. TE's guide puts the levels in the scene; tutorial videos on OS 1.0.x show them following the pattern.","docs/research/65-video-tutorials.md#216-mixer","community-verified",{"id":47,"text":48,"source":49,"firmware_min":27,"verified_on":27,"confidence":33},"master-chain","After the mixer, the summed signal passes through the EQ, then the saturator, then the compressor and limiter, and on to the main output.","https://teenage.engineering/guides/op-xy/mix#signal-flow-chart",{"id":51,"text":52,"source":49,"firmware_min":27,"verified_on":27,"confidence":33},"send-returns","A voice reaches the mixer directly and through its sends to the aux out, tape, FX I and FX II tracks, which feed the mixer as well.",{"id":54,"text":55,"source":49,"firmware_min":27,"verified_on":27,"confidence":33},"send-chain","In TE's signal flow diagram each send track can also feed the next one down — aux out into tape, tape into FX I, FX I into FX II — and no arrow runs back up, so FX II returns only to the mixer.",{"id":57,"text":58,"source":59,"firmware_min":27,"verified_on":27,"confidence":60},"opens-instrument","Opening mix while an auxiliary track is selected shows the instrument tracks first; press mix again to reach the auxiliary tracks (a narrated video, OS 1.0.13).","docs/research/78-overnight-accuracy.md#log","community",[62,68],{"id":63,"goal":64,"preconditions":65,"steps":66,"result":27,"source":32,"firmware_min":27,"verified_on":27,"confidence":33},"enter","Open mix mode",[],[67],{"keys":5,"note":27,"set":27},{"id":69,"goal":70,"preconditions":71,"steps":73,"result":27,"source":37,"firmware_min":27,"verified_on":27,"confidence":33},"track-kind","Switch mix between instrument and auxiliary tracks",[72],"mix mode",[74],{"keys":5,"note":27,"set":27},[],[77,78,79,80,81,82,83],"mix.levels-pans-sends","mix.mute-solo","mix.eq","mix.saturator","mix.master","fx.overview","arrange.scenes","Mix mode has four pages: `M1` is the channel strip of the selected track, and `M2`…`M4` work on the\nmaster — EQ, saturator, then group levels, compressor and output. Tracks reach the mixer directly and\nthrough their sends; the sum then runs through the master chain to the output. Levels and pans travel\nwith each pattern and scenes keep the mutes, so a balance change can be part of the arrangement.",[86,88,89,91,92],{"url":32,"kind":87},"guide",{"url":37,"kind":87},{"url":44,"kind":90},"research",{"url":49,"kind":87},{"url":59,"kind":90},[94],"key.mix",{"id":5,"title":96},"Mix",{"id":77,"title":98},"Levels, pans and sends",{"basics.key-notation":100,"basics.main-modes":101,"basics.modules":102,"basics.track-buttons":103,"basics.linked-tracks":104,"basics.patterns-scenes-songs":105,"basics.workflow":106,"basics.firmware-versions":107,"hardware.layout":108,"hardware.power-and-charging":109,"hardware.connectors":110,"hardware.specifications":111,"hardware.te-boot":112,"hardware.firmware-update":113,"hardware.factory-reset":114,"hardware.system-menu":115,"hardware.safety-and-care":116,"hardware.in-the-box":117,"sequencer.overview":118,"sequencer.step-entry":119,"sequencer.step-recording":120,"sequencer.live-recording":121,"sequencer.extend-notes":122,"sequencer.nudge":123,"sequencer.single-sound":124,"sequencer.rotate":125,"sequencer.copy-step":126,"sequencer.transpose-sequence":127,"sequencer.parameter-locks":128,"sequencer.clear-and-undo":129,"sequencer.step-components":130,"sequencer.step-component-reference":131,"sequencer.component-pulse":132,"sequencer.component-pulse-hold":133,"sequencer.component-multiply":134,"sequencer.component-velocity":135,"sequencer.component-ramp-up":136,"sequencer.component-ramp-down":137,"sequencer.component-random":138,"sequencer.component-portamento":139,"sequencer.component-bend":140,"sequencer.component-tonality":141,"sequencer.component-jump":142,"sequencer.component-skip-parameter-lock":143,"sequencer.component-skip-step-component":144,"sequencer.component-skip-trigger":145,"sequencer.bar-menu":146,"sequencer.track-scale":147,"sequencer.bars-and-length":148,"players.overview":149,"players.arpeggio":150,"players.maestro":151,"players.hold":152,"instrument.ove